KNOWNBUG
increasing-range-part-select1.sv
--module main
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.w\[0\] == 1: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.w\[3:0\] == 4'b1010: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.w\[7:4\] == 4'b0101: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p3\] always main\.w\[2\+:2\] == 2'b10: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p4\] always main\.w\[3-:2\] == 2'b10: PROVED .*$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
For a vector declared with an increasing range, the part-select w[0:3]
denotes the most significant four bits (1800-2017 7.4.1, 11.5.1). The
lowering of part-selects only subtracts the offset of the range, and
does not take the direction of the range into account, and hence
selects the least significant bits. The same applies to indexed
part-selects. Bit-selects are lowered correctly.
